            {"heading": "Managing the Always-On Default", "body": ["The default setting of modern professional life is constant availability. The research on this default is unambiguous: constant connectivity increases cortisol, reduces cognitive performance on complex tasks, degrades sleep quality, and undermines relationship quality.", "Specific boundaries with documented benefit: no work email/apps in the 60 minutes before bed and after waking, phone-free meals (especially with family), designated device-free periods during the day.", "The professional who sets these limits and communicates them clearly is not less committed to their work. They are more effective at it — and they model a sustainable way of working that high-performing teams increasingly need to function without burning out."]},
